1
00:00:00,556 --> 00:00:02,606
Security is not one thing.

2
00:00:03,111 --> 00:00:05,961
It is a set of services a system provides.

3
00:00:06,581 --> 00:00:09,411
X.800 lists six of them.

4
00:00:11,022 --> 00:00:12,272
Authentication.

5
00:00:12,842 --> 00:00:17,392
Assurance that the communicating
entity is the one it claims to be.

6
00:00:17,877 --> 00:00:20,167
Peer authentication for a connection.

7
00:00:20,782 --> 00:00:23,912
Data origin authentication for a message.

8
00:00:25,689 --> 00:00:26,919
Access control.

9
00:00:27,469 --> 00:00:31,039
Protection against
unauthorized use of resources.

10
00:00:31,864 --> 00:00:33,614
Only the right people get in.

11
00:00:36,476 --> 00:00:36,776
Data confidentiality.

12
00:00:37,536 --> 00:00:41,066
Protection of transmitted
data from passive attack.

13
00:00:41,591 --> 00:00:42,441
Whole connection,

14
00:00:42,811 --> 00:00:46,601
single field,
or the fact that traffic exists at all.

15
00:00:49,049 --> 00:00:49,469
Data integrity.

16
00:00:50,014 --> 00:00:54,204
Assurance that the data received
is exactly the data sent.

17
00:00:54,699 --> 00:00:57,609
Nothing added, nothing changed on the way.

18
00:00:59,289 --> 00:01:00,679
Non-repudiation.

19
00:01:01,249 --> 00:01:02,779
Guards against denial.

20
00:01:03,384 --> 00:01:05,334
The sender cannot deny sending.

21
00:01:05,939 --> 00:01:07,969
The receiver cannot deny receipt.

22
00:01:09,756 --> 00:01:11,146
Availability service.

23
00:01:11,846 --> 00:01:16,976
A resource is accessible and usable
by authorized users when needed.

24
00:01:17,431 --> 00:01:19,441
Quality of service matters here.

25
00:01:21,056 --> 00:01:23,886
Six services, each answers one attack.

26
00:01:25,256 --> 00:01:27,306
Confidentiality against eavesdropping.

27
00:01:27,771 --> 00:01:29,961
Integrity against modification.

28
00:01:30,746 --> 00:01:33,536
Availability against denial of service.

29
00:01:34,076 --> 00:01:38,006
Authentication and access
control against masquerade.

30
00:01:38,501 --> 00:01:41,591
Non-repudiation against repudiation.

